# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# Without this, Git's core.autocrlf rewrites files with CRLF on Windows
# checkouts while CI (Linux) sees LF. That splits local and CI results on
# anything line-ending sensitive: `prettier --check` fails locally on files
# that pass in CI, and the API contract drift check
# (.github/workflows/ci.yml) can report a diff on a regenerated file whose
# content is byte-identical. Pinning eol=lf makes both environments agree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated from the backend's OpenAPI schema. Marked explicitly so the
# drift check compares content, never line endings.
frontend/src/types/api.generated.ts text eol=lf
openapi.json text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
